  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "HOUR adds 0.5/86400 (half a second) before extracting the hour, so 0.999999 returns 0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088 and build 20430, HOUR(serial_number) rounds the serial to the nearest second by adding 0.5/86400 before taking the fractional day and multiplying by 24 (the same pre-extraction rounding as MINUTE and SECOND). Thus HOUR(0.999999) (23:59:59.9136) rounds up to 00:00:00 of the next day and returns 0 instead of 23. All 10,153 full-bank HOUR rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (f2_rows row 115) and matched across 10,153/10,153 full-bank HOUR rows (Excel 16.0 build 20430).",
